abstract: "A public technical release of the Recognition Null Kernel Engine (RNKE), a general verification architecture for formalizable claim-evidence-dependency systems. The release includes AI trust-enablement components and a connector-ready, fail-closed Challenge Engine with exploratory, adversarial, and certified modes; mathematical hallucination and formal numeric-overclaim testing; challenge-genesis and evaluation hashing; exact and proof-carrying numerical gates; seam-quotient negative controls; observer-flow probes; burden/reserve checks; and finite-to-limit completion gates. The current public Challenge is a benchmark of RNKE rather than the full scope of the architecture."
